  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5504.08 Waiver of Fee",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5504.08 Waiver of Fee.\n\n(a) If a sexual offender or offender against children cannot afford to pay the registration fee, the offender may request a waiver of the fee and a hearing pursuant to Saf-C 5506.02, on form DSSP 311, within 10 days of registration.\n\n(b) In order to be considered, the sexual offender or offender against children shall complete and submit the financial affidavit form DSSP 358 ‘Affidavit of Assets and Liabilities’, effective November 2022, supplied by the department within 10 days of the request for a waiver.\n\n(c) Pursuant to RSA 651-B:11, II, upon receipt of the offender’s completed financial affidavit form DSSP 358, and after review of the offender’s financial affidavit form DSSP 358, the commissioner shall waive the fee without a hearing if the commissioner determines the offender is indigent as defined by Saf-C 5506.02(a).\n\nSource. #10121, eff 4-25-12; ss by #13504, eff 12-9-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5500.html"
